W:1. Some old Robin down they call me
W:But I'm a weaver by my trade.
W:In this fair berth in which I'm dwelling
W:And Ibby Damsel my heart betrayed.
W:
W:2. Her hair's as black as a raven's feather
W:That do sit on yon willow tree,
W:Her sparkling eyes they're so enticing;
W:But from her chamber I can't get free.
W:
W:3. Her heart as sweet as any posy,
W:Her cheeks are of the rosy red,
W:Her sparkling eyes are so enticing,
W:Her eyebrows wove with a golden thread
%
